  <div class="case-takeaway">
    <h3>Key takeaways</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <div class="tone-junior">Mutation testing catches gaps line coverage can't see, but running it across an entire codebase generates so much low-value noise that teams stop reading the results, and eventually stop running it at all.</div>
        <div class="tone-mid">Scope mutation testing to a small set of genuinely high-risk modules, payments, auth, data integrity, so a real survived mutant is a short, readable report instead of one line in hundreds.</div>
        <div class="tone-staff">Not every survived mutant is a real gap — some are equivalent mutants that can never be killed. Chasing 100% everywhere is its own version of the same overkill; match the mutation score target to where the cost of a gap is genuinely high.</div>
